# Build context for cic/Dockerfile is the REPO ROOT, because the image has
# to reach two trees: cic/ (the serving app and its records) and
# cic-poc/frontend/ (the only participant-facing UI, and the one CI builds).
#
# The repo is 572MB and almost none of it belongs in a build context, so
# this is an allowlist rather than a list of exclusions: deny everything,
# then re-admit the four paths the Dockerfile actually copies. A new
# directory added at the root is excluded by default, which is the right
# way round - a context grows silently otherwise.
*

!cic/
!cic-poc/frontend/

# ...and then the heavy or irrelevant parts of what was just admitted.
# 154MB of primary-source texts; nothing under runtime/app/ reads them.
cic/texts/
# CI-only gates. They run in GitHub Actions against the repo, never in
# the served container.
cic/checks/
# Generated at build time by runtime/scripts/build_indices.py. A
# host-built copy must never be admitted - the image has to contain
# indices built against the records in THIS image.
cic/runtime/vector_store/
# Ephemeral session logs. Never seed a container with someone else's.
cic/runtime/transcripts/

# Installed and built inside the frontend stage, never copied in.
cic-poc/frontend/node_modules/
cic-poc/frontend/dist/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.DS_Store
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
